@*
    UnderConstruction — the four operational pages that have tables but no
    behaviour yet.

    Written as a status, not an apology. Each one says which part of the
    platform it stands for and what is true today, then points at the two
    places in the console that do work — an empty screen should be an
    invitation to act, and "coming soon" is not one.

    The mark is an unpopulated array: the same panel grid the Overview nav icon
    draws, with its cells left as dashed outlines. It is the subject of this
    business with nothing in it yet, which is exactly the state being reported.
*@

<div class="soon">
    <svg class="soon__mark" width="64" height="64" viewBox="0 0 24 24"
         fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25"
         stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
         aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="13" rx="1.5" stroke-dasharray="2.5 2" />
        <path d="M9 4v13M15 4v13M3 8.3h18M3 12.7h18" stroke-dasharray="2.5 2" />
        <path d="M12 17v3M8 20h8" />
    </svg>

    <div>
        <p class="soon__title">@Title</p>
        <p class="soon__body">@Body</p>
    </div>

    <div class="soon__links">
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="manage">Go to the dashboard</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="manage/activity-logs">Open the activity log</a>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Body { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
